      "files": {
        "1": {
          "id": "1",
          "name": "index.html",
          "language": "html",
          "contents": "<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n  <meta charset=\"utf-8\" />\n  <title>Lesson 7 · Exposure Meter</title>\n  <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1\" />\n  <link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"style.css\" />\n  <script defer src=\"script.js\"></script>\n</head>\n<body>\n  <div class=\"wrap\">\n    <header>\n      <h1>Campus Life · Exposure Meter</h1>\n      <p>Explore how the first N items of a feed shape what people see. Adjust controls. Judge clarity, readability, accessibility, and fairness.</p>\n      <div class=\"toolbar\" role=\"group\" aria-label=\"Display options\">\n        <label><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"toggle-contrast\" /> High contrast</label>\n        <label><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"big-text\" /> Larger text</label>\n      </div>\n    </header>\n\n    <div class=\"grid\">\n      <main class=\"panel\" id=\"left\">\n        <h2>Campus Life Feed</h2>\n\n        <div class=\"controls\" aria-label=\"Meter controls\">\n          <div>\n            <label for=\"nValue\">Count first N posts</label>\n            <input id=\"nValue\" type=\"number\" min=\"1\" step=\"1\" value=\"8\" />\n          </div>\n          <div>\n            <label for=\"categoryLabels\">Category labels shown to users</label>\n            <input id=\"categoryLabels\" type=\"text\" value=\"sports, arts, academics, service\" />\n          </div>\n        </div>\n\n        <div class=\"toolbar\" role=\"group\" aria-label=\"Feed tools\">\n          <button id=\"shuffle\">Shuffle order</button>\n          <button id=\"reset\" class=\"secondary\">Reset order</button>\n        </div>\n\n        <section id=\"feed\" class=\"feed\" aria-label=\"Campus Life cards\">\n          <!-- Cards injected by script.js -->\n        </section>\n      </main>\n\n      <aside class=\"panel\" id=\"right\" aria-labelledby=\"meter-title\">\n        <h2 id=\"meter-title\">Exposure Meter</h2>\n\n        <div class=\"meter\" aria-live=\"polite\" aria-atomic=\"true\">\n          <div><span class=\"pill\" id=\"meter-pill\">0 of 0 counted</span></div>\n          <div class=\"counts\" id=\"counts\"></div>\n          <p id=\"summary\" class=\"muted\"></p>\n          <p id=\"fairness\" class=\"note okay\"></p>\n          <p id=\"live-status\" class=\"sr-only\" aria-live=\"polite\"></p>\n        </div>\n\n        <hr />\n\n        <section aria-labelledby=\"revise-title\">\n          <h3 id=\"revise-title\">Revise labels for clarity</h3>\n          <p class=\"small\">Try renaming a category to make meaning clearer or more inclusive.</p>\n          <div class=\"controls\">\n            <div>\n              <label for=\"renameFrom\">Old label</label>\n              <input id=\"renameFrom\" type=\"text\" placeholder=\"sports\" />\n            </div>\n            <div>\n              <label for=\"renameTo\">New label</label>\n              <input id=\"renameTo\" type=\"text\" placeholder=\"athletics\" />\n            </div>\n          </div>\n          <button id=\"applyRename\">Apply label change</button>\n        </section>\n      </aside>\n    </div>\n\n    <section class=\"panel\" style=\"margin-top:1rem\">\n      <h2>Notes for analysis</h2>\n      <ul class=\"small\">\n        <li>Use the high contrast and larger text toggles to judge readability and accessibility.</li>\n        <li>Shuffle the feed to see how order reshapes the first N items.</li>\n        <li>Watch the fairness note. If one category dominates, consider a fairer default.</li>\n      </ul>\n    </section>\n  </div>\n</body>\n</html>\n",
          "active": false,
          "folderId": "0"
        },
        "2": {
          "id": "2",
          "name": "style.css",
          "language": "css",
          "contents": ":root {\n  --bg: #f6f7fb;\n  --ink: #111;\n  --ink-soft: #333;\n  --panel: #fff;\n  --accent: #4b6bfb;\n  --muted: #8a93a0;\n  --card: #fff;\n  --card-border: #e5e7eb;\n  --focus: #111;\n}\n\n* { box-sizing: border-box; }\n\nbody {\n  margin: 0;\n  font-family: system-ui, -apple-system, Segoe UI, Roboto, \"Helvetica Neue\", Arial, \"Noto Sans\", \"Liberation Sans\", sans-serif;\n  color: var(--ink);\n  background: var(--bg);\n  line-height: 1.5;\n}\n\n.wrap {\n  max-width: 1100px;\n  margin: 0 auto;\n  padding: 1rem;\n}\n\nheader h1 {\n  margin: 0.25rem 0 0.25rem;\n  font-size: 1.4rem;\n}\nheader p {\n  margin: 0;\n  color: var(--muted);\n  font-size: 0.95rem;\n}\n\n.grid {\n  display: grid;\n  grid-template-columns: 1fr 360px;\n  gap: 1rem;\n  margin-top: 1rem;\n}\n@media (max-width: 960px) {\n  .grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }\n}\n\n.panel {\n  background: var(--panel);\n  border: 1px solid #e6e6e6;\n  border-radius: 12px;\n  padding: 1rem;\n  box-shadow: 0 0.25rem 0.5rem rgba(0,0,0,0.04);\n}\n.panel h2 {\n  margin-top: 0;\n  font-size: 1.1rem;\n}\n.panel h3 {\n  margin-bottom: 0.25rem;\n  font-size: 1rem;\n}\n\n.controls {\n  display: grid;\n  grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;\n  gap: 0.5rem;\n  margin: 0.5rem 0 0.75rem;\n}\n\nlabel { font-weight: 600; font-size: 0.9rem; }\n\ninput[type=\"number\"],\ninput[type=\"text\"],\ntextarea {\n  width: 100%;\n  padding: 0.5rem 0.6rem;\n  border: 1px solid #cfd3da;\n  border-radius: 8px;\n  font: inherit;\n  background: #fff;\n  color: var(--ink);\n}\n\nbutton {\n  appearance: none;\n  border: 0;\n  border-radius: 10px;\n  padding: 0.55rem 0.8rem;\n  background: var(--accent);\n  color: #fff;\n  font-weight: 600;\n  cursor: pointer;\n}\nbutton.secondary {\n  background: #e9ecf7;\n  color: #1c2a62;\n}\nbutton:focus-visible, input:focus-visible, textarea:focus-visible {\n  outline: 3px solid var(--focus);\n  outline-offset: 2px;\n}\n\n.feed {\n  display: grid;\n  grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(240px, 1fr));\n  gap: 0.75rem;\n}\n.card {\n  background: var(--card);\n  border: 1px solid var(--card-border);\n  border-radius: 12px;\n  padding: 0.8rem;\n}\n.card h4 {\n  margin: 0 0 0.25rem;\n  font-size: 1rem;\n}\n.tag {\n  display: inline-block;\n  padding: 0.1rem 0.5rem;\n  border-radius: 999px;\n  font-size: 0.75rem;\n  border: 1px solid #d7dbe4;\n  color: var(--ink-soft);\n}\n.order {\n  font-size: 0.75rem;\n  color: var(--muted);\n}\n\n.meter {\n  display: grid;\n  gap: 0.5rem;\n}\n.pill {\n  display: inline-block;\n  padding: 0.2rem 0.6rem;\n  border-radius: 999px;\n  background: #eef2ff;\n  color: #233089;\n  font-weight: 700;\n  font-size: 0.85rem;\n}\n.counts {\n  display: grid;\n  grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;\n  gap: 0.25rem 0.5rem;\n  align-items: baseline;\n}\n.counts div { display: contents; }\n.counts span.label { color: var(--ink-soft); }\n\n.note {\n  padding: 0.6rem 0.7rem;\n  border-radius: 8px;\n  background: #fff7ed;\n  border: 1px solid #fde6c7;\n  color: #7a4a07;\n  font-size: 0.9rem;\n}\n.okay {\n  background: #f0fdf4;\n  border: 1px solid #bbf7d0;\n  color: #14532d;\n}\n\n.muted { color: var(--muted); font-size: 0.9rem; }\n\n.toolbar {\n  display: flex;\n  gap: 0.5rem;\n  align-items: center;\n  flex-wrap: wrap;\n  margin: 0.25rem 0 0.75rem;\n}\n\n.sr-only {\n  position: absolute; width: 1px; height: 1px; padding: 0; margin: -1px;\n  overflow: hidden; clip: rect(0,0,0,0); border: 0;\n}\n\n/* High contrast mode */\n.high-contrast {\n  --bg: #ffffff;\n  --ink: #000;\n  --panel: #fff;\n  --accent: #000;\n  --card-border: #000;\n  --focus: #000;\n}\n\n.small { font-size: 0.85rem; color: var(--muted); }\n",
          "folderId": "0",
          "active": false
        },
        "3": {
          "id": "3",
          "name": "script.js",
          "language": "js",
          "contents": "// Tiny helpers\nconst $ = sel => document.querySelector(sel);\n\n// Feed data\nconst originalFeed = [\n  { id: 1,  title: \"Varsity Game Highlights\", category: \"sports\", blurb: \"Photo set from last night.\" },\n  { id: 2,  title: \"Spring Musical Rehearsal\", category: \"arts\", blurb: \"Backstage snapshots.\" },\n  { id: 3,  title: \"Math Team Regionals\", category: \"academics\", blurb: \"Qualifiers posted.\" },\n  { id: 4,  title: \"Track Meet Results\", category: \"sports\", blurb: \"Personal records.\" },\n  { id: 5,  title: \"Volunteers Needed\", category: \"service\", blurb: \"Food pantry Saturday.\" },\n  { id: 6,  title: \"Choir Festival\", category: \"arts\", blurb: \"Set list released.\" },\n  { id: 7,  title: \"Soccer Tryouts\", category: \"sports\", blurb: \"Times and sign-up.\" },\n  { id: 8,  title: \"Robotics Demo Day\", category: \"academics\", blurb: \"Open lab tours.\" },\n  { id: 9,  title: \"Tutoring Schedule\", category: \"academics\", blurb: \"After-school help.\" },\n  { id: 10, title: \"Campus Cleanup Photos\", category: \"service\", blurb: \"Thanks to all teams.\" },\n  { id: 11, title: \"Art Show Winners\", category: \"arts\", blurb: \"Congrats to featured artists.\" },\n  { id: 12, title: \"Basketball Fundraiser\", category: \"sports\", blurb: \"Community night.\" }\n];\nlet feed = originalFeed.map(x => ({...x}));\n\n// Display labels that students can revise\nconst labels = new Map([\n  [\"sports\", \"sports\"],\n  [\"arts\", \"arts\"],\n  [\"academics\", \"academics\"],\n  [\"service\", \"service\"]\n]);\n\n// Render the feed grid\nfunction renderFeed() {\n  const container = $(\"#feed\");\n  container.innerHTML = feed.map((item, idx) => `\n    <article class=\"card\" aria-labelledby=\"card-${item.id}-title\">\n      <div class=\"order\">#${idx + 1}</div>\n      <h4 id=\"card-${item.id}-title\">${item.title}</h4>\n      <p><span class=\"tag\" aria-label=\"Category\">${labels.get(item.category)}</span></p>\n      <p class=\"muted\">${item.blurb}</p>\n    </article>\n  `).join(\"\");\n}\n\n// Slice first N posts\nfunction firstN(n) {\n  const num = Math.max(1, Math.min(n, feed.length));\n  return feed.slice(0, num);\n}\n\n// Tally by category\nfunction tallyCounts(n) {\n  const items = firstN(n);\n  const counts = {};\n  items.forEach(item => {\n    const cat = item.category;\n    counts[cat] = (counts[cat] || 0) + 1;\n  });\n  return { counts, total: items.length };\n}\n\n// Find dominating category share\nfunction topShare(counts, total) {\n  let maxCat = null;\n  let maxVal = -1;\n  Object.keys(counts).forEach(k => {\n    if (counts[k] > maxVal) { maxVal = counts[k]; maxCat = k; }\n  });\n  const share = total > 0 ? (maxVal / total) : 0;\n  return { maxCat, maxVal, share };\n}\n\n// Human summary sentence\nfunction humanSummary(counts, total) {\n  const parts = Object.keys(counts).sort().map(k => `${labels.get(k) || k}: ${counts[k]}`);\n  return `In the first ${total} posts → ${parts.join(\", \")}.`;\n}\n\n// Update the meter panel\nfunction renderMeter() {\n  const n = parseInt($(\"#nValue\").value, 10);\n  const { counts, total } = tallyCounts(n);\n\n  $(\"#meter-pill\").textContent = `${total} of ${feed.length} counted`;\n\n  const allCats = ($(\"#categoryLabels\").value || \"\")\n    .split(\",\")\n    .map(s => s.trim())\n    .filter(Boolean);\n\n  const knownKeys = Object.keys(counts);\n  const displayCats = allCats.length ? allCats : knownKeys;\n\n  $(\"#counts\").innerHTML = displayCats.map(cat => {\n    const key = cat.toLowerCase();\n    const count = counts[key] || 0;\n    const name = labels.get(key) || cat;\n    return `<div><span class=\"label\">${name}</span><span>${count}</span></div>`;\n  }).join(\"\");\n\n  $(\"#summary\").textContent = humanSummary(counts, total);\n\n  const { maxCat, share, maxVal } = topShare(counts, total);\n  const fairnessBox = $(\"#fairness\");\n\n  if (share >= 0.5 && maxCat) {\n    const pretty = labels.get(maxCat) || maxCat;\n    fairnessBox.className = \"note\";\n    fairnessBox.textContent = `${pretty} dominates the first ${total} posts (${maxVal}/${total}). Consider a fairer default.`;\n  } else {\n    fairnessBox.className = \"note okay\";\n    fairnessBox.textContent = \"Balance looks reasonable in the first N posts.\";\n  }\n\n  $(\"#live-status\").textContent = `Exposure counts updated for first ${total} posts.`;\n}\n\n// Sync display labels with the text field\nfunction syncLabelsFromInput() {\n  const raw = ($(\"#categoryLabels\").value || \"\")\n    .split(\",\")\n    .map(s => s.trim().toLowerCase())\n    .filter(Boolean);\n\n  raw.forEach(text => {\n    const key = text.toLowerCase();\n    if (labels.has(key)) labels.set(key, text);\n  });\n}\n\n// Shuffle and reset helpers\nfunction shuffleArray(arr) {\n  for (let i = arr.length - 1; i > 0; i--) {\n    const j = Math.floor(Math.random() * (i + 1));\n    [arr[i], arr[j]] = [arr[j], arr[i]];\n  }\n}\n\n// Event wiring\n$(\"#nValue\").addEventListener(\"input\", renderMeter);\n\n$(\"#categoryLabels\").addEventListener(\"change\", () => {\n  syncLabelsFromInput();\n  renderFeed();\n  renderMeter();\n});\n\n$(\"#toggle-contrast\").addEventListener(\"change\", e => {\n  document.body.classList.toggle(\"high-contrast\", e.target.checked);\n});\n\n$(\"#big-text\").addEventListener(\"change\", e => {\n  document.body.style.fontSize = e.target.checked ? \"18px\" : \"\";\n});\n\n$(\"#applyRename\").addEventListener(\"click\", () => {\n  const from = ($(\"#renameFrom\").value || \"\").trim().toLowerCase();\n  const to = ($(\"#renameTo\").value || \"\").trim();\n  if (!from || !to) return;\n  if (labels.has(from)) {\n    labels.set(from, to);\n\n    // reflect in the categoryLabels input if present\n    const parts = ($(\"#categoryLabels\").value || \"\").split(\",\").map(s => s.trim());\n    const idx = parts.findIndex(p => p.toLowerCase() === from);\n    if (idx !== -1) {\n      parts[idx] = to;\n      $(\"#categoryLabels\").value = parts.join(\", \");\n    }\n\n    renderFeed();\n    renderMeter();\n  }\n});\n\n$(\"#shuffle\").addEventListener(\"click\", () => {\n  shuffleArray(feed);\n  renderFeed();\n  renderMeter();\n});\n\n$(\"#reset\").addEventListener(\"click\", () => {\n  feed = originalFeed.map(x => ({...x}));\n  renderFeed();\n  renderMeter();\n});\n\n// First paint\nrenderFeed();\nrenderMeter();\n",
          "folderId": "0",
          "active": false
        },
        "4": {
          "id": "4",
          "name": "progression.md",
          "language": "md",
          "contents": "# Lesson 7 · Activity Progression\nCampus Life Exposure Meter\n\nYou will use the web app to investigate how a feed’s first N items shape what people see. Follow the steps, record observations, and turn feedback into prompts you can test.\n\n---\n\n## 1) Warm start\n- Set **N** to 8.\n- Read the **pill** text and the **summary** sentence.\n- Ask yourself: is the display clear at a glance, or do I need to hunt for meaning? [1]\n\n---\n\n## 2) Clarity, readability, and accessibility checklist [1]\nUse the toggles and the interface to test the display, then note issues and improvements.\n\n- Toggle **High contrast**. Confirm text and outlines remain readable.\n- Toggle **Larger text**. Confirm the layout holds and nothing important is cut off.\n- Scan heading order: title → region headings → cards. Confirm a logical reading flow.\n- Check the **counts grid**. Can you match labels to numbers without guessing?\n- Read the **summary** aloud. Does it say who gets what, in plain language, within one breath?\n- Listen for updates: the page announces count changes in a live region. Does it help?\n\n**Prompt pattern to address a finding**\n> Improve the summary for clarity by rewriting it in under 18 words. Preserve counts. Output one sentence only.\n\n---\n\n## 3) Bias and perspective scan [2]\nYou are looking for dominance, omission, and framing.\n\n- Press **Shuffle**. Recompute. Repeat three times. Does a category keep appearing first?\n- Watch the **fairness note**. If one group is at least 50 percent of the first N, the note warns you.\n- Ask what is missing. Which groups or activities do not show in the top N at all?\n- Consider order effects. If two sports posts sit first, how many clicks do arts or service lose?\n- Name a perspective that might feel excluded and why.\n\n**Prompt pattern to explore balance**\n> Suggest one default that reduces repetition in the first N posts. Provide a single sentence and a short example.\n\n---\n\n## 4) Label and display revisions for inclusivity and accuracy [3]\nLabels shape meaning. Test small changes and measure the result.\n\n- Rename a label in the sidebar. Example: change **sports** to **athletics** if that reads wider.\n- Rerun the meter. Does the new wording improve comprehension or neutrality?\n- Check plural vs singular. Choose the form that matches how a student would say it.\n- Replace niche jargon. Use terms that a ninth grader understands.\n- Add a short rationale. Why is the new label clearer or more inclusive?\n\n**Prompt pattern to refine labels**\n> Propose three alternative labels for \"<current label>\" that are clear to ninth graders. Explain each in one clause.\n\n---\n\n## 5) Build prompts through CHAT\nYou will not see these steps in the app. Use them to structure your AI requests and your tests.\n\n### C · Clarify\n- State the goal, inputs, where results appear, and how you will check success.\n- Example:\n  > Count the first <N> items by category and update the pill, counts grid, and summary. Confirm that totals change when N changes.\n\n### H · Hone\n- Add one improvement such as a fairness nudge or a simpler sentence.\n- Example:\n  > If any category is at least 50 percent of the first N, add a short fairness note with one suggestion.\n\n### A · Apply\n- Run your change in the page. Shuffle. Adjust N. Verify behavior and record pass or miss.\n- Example verification notes:\n  - Pill updates when N changes. Pass.\n  - Fairness note shows only when a category is 50 percent or more. Pass.\n  - Summary exceeds 18 words. Miss. Needs edit.\n\n### T · Transfer\n- Turn your working idea into a reusable template with placeholders.\n- Template starter:\n  1) Goal: summarize balance for the first `<N>` items in a feed.  \n  2) Inputs: array of `{ id, title, category }`, label map, `<N>`.  \n  3) Rules: use plain words, keep sentences short, add fairness n\n",
          "folderId": "0",
          "active": true
        }
      },
